WEBVTT

00:14.896 --> 00:17.190
It's spring break!

00:17.858 --> 00:19.317
You sure are cheerful, Miki.

00:19.401 --> 00:20.569
Who wouldn't be? Look.

00:20.652 --> 00:22.821
We're at a theme park!

00:23.405 --> 00:25.073
Exams are over,
and spring break has begun.

00:25.157 --> 00:28.910
What's a better way to spend it
than hanging out with friends?

00:28.994 --> 00:32.122
This is what high school's about!

00:32.205 --> 00:35.125
Hey, guys! Thanks for waiting.

00:35.208 --> 00:36.334
There you are.

00:36.418 --> 00:38.503
Heya, Minato and Yota.

00:39.004 --> 00:40.338
Sorry, did we keep you waiting?

00:40.422 --> 00:41.423
Nope.

00:41.506 --> 00:42.591
Huh?

00:43.341 --> 00:46.845
What's this, Minato?
Your outfit's on point today!

00:47.512 --> 00:50.223
I've only seen you in casual outfits.

00:50.307 --> 00:51.933
LIVE FEED - MINATO'S ROOM
MESSY

00:52.017 --> 00:53.351
<i>This is my casual fit.</i>

00:54.311 --> 00:56.646
- Well, shall we get going?
- Wait for me, Minato.

00:56.730 --> 00:57.731
POWER WALKING

00:57.814 --> 00:59.608
Let's go, Koyun.

00:59.691 --> 01:00.776
Okay.

01:00.859 --> 01:04.863
<i>At Miki's suggestion,</i>
<i>the four of us came to the theme park.</i>

02:36.538 --> 02:40.959
EPISODE 10
SPRING

02:41.042 --> 02:42.210
ENTRANCE

02:42.294 --> 02:45.422
Glad it's a nice, warm day.

02:45.505 --> 02:48.341
I love the feeling of the season changing.

02:48.425 --> 02:49.718
I know what you mean.

02:49.801 --> 02:51.011
MEMORIES TIED TO THE CLIMATE

02:51.094 --> 02:52.888
It reminds me of the entrance ceremony.

02:52.971 --> 02:53.972
MEMORIES - CLIMATE

02:54.055 --> 02:56.600
It takes me back
to the day my younger siblings were born.

02:58.059 --> 03:00.353
Were you and your siblings born in spring?

03:00.437 --> 03:02.856
Yep, all April babies.

03:02.939 --> 03:07.277
Koyun, your birthday's in February,
so you're almost a full year younger.

03:07.360 --> 03:08.862
You're right.

03:08.945 --> 03:12.365
February? That's pretty recent.
You should've told us.

03:14.284 --> 03:15.619
Was I supposed to?

03:16.202 --> 03:17.495
SHOCK

03:17.579 --> 03:20.749
Excuse me. Can I get a birthday sticker?

03:20.832 --> 03:21.917
Here you go.

03:22.000 --> 03:23.251
But my birthday was last month--

03:23.335 --> 03:24.669
STICK

03:27.505 --> 03:29.007
Look over there.

03:29.090 --> 03:30.175
PHOTO SHOOT OK!
ZONED OUT

03:30.258 --> 03:32.510
The mascot looks bored.
Let's have it celebrate you.

03:33.178 --> 03:35.555
Celebrate me?
And what's that thing supposed to be?

03:35.639 --> 03:37.557
Don't be shy. Go, go, go.

03:40.227 --> 03:44.231
<i>Seriously, Yota… he's such a dad.</i>

03:44.856 --> 03:45.941
There.

03:47.025 --> 03:49.736
- Dance with me.
- It's a bunny.

03:49.819 --> 03:51.738
Uppi, uppi!

03:51.821 --> 03:52.822
That's wacky.

03:52.906 --> 03:54.115
<i>- Someone help…</i>
- Uppi!

03:56.117 --> 03:57.202
SNAP, SNAP

03:57.285 --> 03:58.286
I endorse this coupling.

04:00.038 --> 04:02.624
Look, they're selling a ton of merch.

04:02.707 --> 04:07.170
I'm kinda into this cheesy merch.

04:09.047 --> 04:11.132
Cheesy?

04:11.216 --> 04:12.634
UPPI BADGE SET
680 YEN (WITHOUT TAX)

04:12.717 --> 04:14.886
- Thank you.
- Uppippi!

04:14.970 --> 04:17.389
The mascot's the cashier?

04:17.973 --> 04:21.142
I got some cute merch. Now I'm satisfied.

04:21.226 --> 04:23.144
Hold on, what about the rides?

04:23.228 --> 04:26.147
We haven't been on a single ride
since we got here.

04:26.231 --> 04:28.525
No way! But we're having so much fun.

04:29.025 --> 04:30.485
Then what if we go do that one?

04:30.986 --> 04:32.904
HOUSE OF HORRORS

04:34.990 --> 04:36.533
No!

04:36.616 --> 04:38.285
Calm down, Miki.

04:38.368 --> 04:39.953
It's just a prop. You're okay.

04:40.036 --> 04:42.914
Koyun, no need to call it what it is.

04:45.250 --> 04:47.752
I know what happens.
When we walk past the coffins,

04:47.836 --> 04:50.547
the lids will swing open. I'm so done!

04:50.630 --> 04:52.924
You'll be fine. Here, look.

04:55.760 --> 04:56.761
HORROR

04:56.845 --> 04:58.805
<i>They put a lot of effort into this.</i>

04:59.306 --> 05:00.932
<i>This is right up Tsukiko's alley.</i>

05:01.975 --> 05:03.810
This skull looks very realistic.

05:04.311 --> 05:05.478
Right, Amamiya--

05:06.646 --> 05:08.732
Don't look, don't look, don't look…

05:08.815 --> 05:09.816
I can't even!

05:12.402 --> 05:15.488
Take me away, Yota.

05:15.572 --> 05:17.324
Sure. Yeah, okay.

05:18.158 --> 05:19.159
CRASH

05:19.242 --> 05:20.243
DROOP

05:20.327 --> 05:21.328
ROUTE

05:21.411 --> 05:22.829
Yota, that way to the exit.

05:22.912 --> 05:25.081
EXIT

05:29.169 --> 05:31.546
Moving on! On to the next one!

05:31.629 --> 05:33.089
<i>She's back to life.</i>

05:42.557 --> 05:43.850
Yay!

05:45.810 --> 05:46.811
Yeah!

05:51.983 --> 05:52.984
Yes!

05:53.068 --> 05:55.653
Let's do this one together next.
It's their main attraction.

05:55.737 --> 05:57.155
FAMOUS CYCLE MONORAIL
SCENIC VIEW

05:57.238 --> 05:58.239
I'll pass.

05:58.323 --> 05:59.324
UGH…

05:59.407 --> 06:01.576
Sorry. I need a break.

06:01.659 --> 06:02.660
Me too.

06:03.620 --> 06:06.039
Guess all that spinning got to me.

06:06.122 --> 06:07.165
Same here.

06:07.248 --> 06:08.249
So…

06:08.333 --> 06:10.668
sorry, but the two of you go on ahead.

06:10.752 --> 06:11.753
THE TWO OF YOU

06:12.337 --> 06:13.671
<i>Koyun!</i>

06:13.755 --> 06:17.717
Looks like the wait time's much longer
than we thought, Yota.

06:20.136 --> 06:21.471
Whoa, hey!

06:24.390 --> 06:25.767
Watch your step!

06:26.351 --> 06:27.519
Sorry.

06:27.602 --> 06:28.770
It's fine.

06:30.438 --> 06:31.523
<i>How do I put it…</i>

06:32.148 --> 06:33.525
<i>Yota's a bit…</i>

06:39.447 --> 06:42.534
The sea. It's glimmering!

06:42.617 --> 06:45.620
I get a bit nervous if I look down.

06:45.703 --> 06:49.040
<i>He seems put together,</i>
<i>but he's actually pretty spacey.</i>

06:49.124 --> 06:51.584
<i>He's like a big baby.</i>

06:57.715 --> 06:59.300
<i>Miki and Yota,</i>

07:00.051 --> 07:02.470
<i>they looked like a couple enjoying a date.</i>

07:06.516 --> 07:08.726
<i>Huh? This situation's like…</i>

07:08.810 --> 07:09.811
BA-BUMP

07:09.894 --> 07:11.229
<i>It's as if we're on a date--</i>

07:11.312 --> 07:12.522
Amamiya.

07:13.231 --> 07:16.192
Do you feel a bit sick today?

07:16.734 --> 07:17.986
Are we pushing you too hard?

07:18.069 --> 07:19.154
Not in the slightest.

07:19.737 --> 07:20.989
I've felt great all day.

07:21.072 --> 07:22.073
UPPI SAMBA

07:22.157 --> 07:23.158
Yeah?

07:23.241 --> 07:24.742
IN FACT, HE WAS EXCITED
SINCE YESTERDAY

07:24.826 --> 07:26.244
I got a little queasy is all.

07:26.327 --> 07:28.496
<i>Huh… Then, maybe he's…</i>

07:29.080 --> 07:32.375
Hey. I wanna play that game while we wait.

07:35.879 --> 07:38.798
Do you go to the arcade a lot?

07:38.882 --> 07:40.842
Yeah, I like 'em.

07:41.342 --> 07:42.719
Watch me.

07:44.429 --> 07:45.513
<i>He's a playful guy.</i>

07:47.348 --> 07:48.600
There!

07:49.517 --> 07:50.810
Strike!

07:50.894 --> 07:52.729
You got it on your first try.

07:52.812 --> 07:55.023
We've got a winner!

07:55.106 --> 07:57.484
Pick one prize from here.

07:57.567 --> 07:58.860
UPPI

07:58.943 --> 08:00.320
<i>It's full of that mascot thing…</i>

08:01.529 --> 08:02.697
PRIZES

08:02.780 --> 08:03.907
Now that's cute.

08:05.492 --> 08:06.910
I'll take that one.

08:06.993 --> 08:07.994
All right.

08:08.995 --> 08:11.581
<i>Amamiya has a real dog at home.</i>

08:11.664 --> 08:12.832
A REAL DOG

08:12.916 --> 08:16.336
- <i>We went off of my preference.</i>
- Here.

08:16.419 --> 08:17.587
PUFFY

08:18.755 --> 08:19.797
You can have it.

08:22.091 --> 08:25.094
Happy birthday, Koyun.

08:27.472 --> 08:28.973
Huh? What?

08:29.057 --> 08:30.558
Huh? What?

08:30.642 --> 08:32.560
NOT USED TO BEING CELEBRATED

08:33.520 --> 08:34.521
What?

08:35.563 --> 08:37.565
PUFFY - FLUFFY

08:38.107 --> 08:39.484
FUZZY…

08:41.694 --> 08:42.695
Thanks.

08:45.323 --> 08:47.158
CLENCH

08:47.242 --> 08:49.244
When's your birthday, Amamiya?

08:49.327 --> 08:51.162
Will you do something for me?

08:51.246 --> 08:52.247
SWOOSH

08:52.330 --> 08:54.249
No, don't expect anything special…

08:57.752 --> 08:59.254
There you are.

08:59.337 --> 09:00.338
BAM

09:00.421 --> 09:01.965
What the heck happened?

09:06.052 --> 09:07.470
SEE YOU NEXT TIME

09:07.554 --> 09:09.013
That was a blast.

09:09.597 --> 09:11.933
Where do you wanna go for dinner?

09:12.016 --> 09:13.601
I'll look up some places.
What kind of food?

09:13.685 --> 09:14.686
STARE - PET, PET

09:14.769 --> 09:16.521
- We walked a lot today.
- Say…

09:16.604 --> 09:18.356
If I'm picking,
then I want to pile up on meat.

09:18.439 --> 09:19.649
<i>What is it?</i>

09:19.732 --> 09:21.859
Are you maybe…

09:22.944 --> 09:24.529
not good with horror?

09:26.656 --> 09:27.907
Right, Amamiya--

09:29.075 --> 09:30.994
DEAD SILENT

09:31.619 --> 09:33.496
AGAPE…

09:35.039 --> 09:37.500
What? What gives you that idea?

09:38.835 --> 09:41.004
Huh? Hold on.

09:41.087 --> 09:43.298
How'd you know? Was it that obvious?

09:44.090 --> 09:45.883
I mean…

09:45.967 --> 09:49.095
I thought it'd be
something for little kids.

09:49.721 --> 09:52.473
Man, this is embarrassing…

09:52.557 --> 09:56.477
<i>Maybe because his reaction</i>
<i>was contrary to my expectation…</i>

09:57.478 --> 10:00.106
Hey… Why're you looking at me like that?

10:01.399 --> 10:02.650
Sorry, it's just…

10:03.234 --> 10:04.694
"It's just…" what?

10:05.820 --> 10:07.155
Wait up.

10:07.238 --> 10:08.448
POWER WALKING
RUNNING AWAY - GIGGLE

10:08.531 --> 10:10.158
- That's mean.
- She's fast.

10:10.742 --> 10:12.869
<i>For the first time in my life,</i>

10:13.369 --> 10:15.371
<i>I thought a guy was cute.</i>

10:15.997 --> 10:17.999
NEW SEMESTER

10:22.003 --> 10:23.504
GRADE 2, CLASS 2

10:31.471 --> 10:32.847
Koyuki.

10:33.348 --> 10:35.016
Good morning.

10:35.683 --> 10:37.018
Tsukiko.

10:37.602 --> 10:39.854
I'm glad we're in the same class again.

10:39.937 --> 10:41.522
I'm looking forward
to being your classmate.

10:41.606 --> 10:42.774
Me too.

10:42.857 --> 10:45.735
Not many of the students in this class
are from Grade 1, Class 2.

10:45.818 --> 10:48.112
I hardly recognize anyone.
I'm a bit nervous.

10:48.696 --> 10:50.531
Do you know anyone?

10:50.615 --> 10:52.325
Yeah, I see a few familiar faces…

10:52.408 --> 10:53.785
Koyun.

10:54.452 --> 10:55.787
Morning.

10:56.579 --> 10:57.789
Morning, Yota.

11:00.625 --> 11:03.044
How nice, you're so tall!

11:03.127 --> 11:04.545
SHE ADMIRES TALL PEOPLE

11:04.629 --> 11:07.048
- I know exactly how you feel.
- Wait, what?

11:08.549 --> 11:09.676
Yota.

11:09.759 --> 11:11.552
Hey, Minato. Good morning.

11:11.636 --> 11:12.762
Good morning.

11:13.388 --> 11:14.681
Good morning to you too, Koyun--

11:15.556 --> 11:17.558
Yes! You're all here!

11:17.642 --> 11:20.103
This isn't a dream, right?

11:20.186 --> 11:22.522
We're all in the same class, right?

11:22.605 --> 11:24.941
- You're not dreaming. Morning.
- Good morning.

11:25.900 --> 11:27.819
Wait, this means you're…

11:28.444 --> 11:30.446
Grade 2, Class 2, Number 2.

11:30.530 --> 11:32.281
Meow, meow, meow.

11:32.365 --> 11:33.658
Meow.

11:33.741 --> 11:36.953
Since I'm Grade 2, Class 2, Number 22…

11:37.036 --> 11:38.496
You're a meow, meow, meow, meow!

11:39.539 --> 11:41.791
<i>It's Azumi!</i>

11:42.417 --> 11:45.086
<i>But Azumi…</i>

11:48.881 --> 11:50.883
<i>isn't quite how I expected her to be.</i>

11:52.051 --> 11:55.221
It's great to meet you. I'm Miki.

11:56.264 --> 11:59.100
You're… You're so cool.

11:59.183 --> 12:02.603
SO COOL

12:02.687 --> 12:03.688
THRILLED - SQUEEZE

12:03.771 --> 12:04.939
Squeeze!

12:05.022 --> 12:06.858
Good for you, Miki.

12:06.941 --> 12:09.777
- I couldn't stop myself from hugging you.
- Azumi…

12:09.861 --> 12:12.363
She's like a completely different person
from last year.

12:12.447 --> 12:15.116
She was your hopes and dreams, huh?

12:15.700 --> 12:17.368
Minato.

12:17.452 --> 12:19.662
Can you do something about him?

12:19.745 --> 12:22.582
Why am I the only one
in a different class?

12:22.665 --> 12:23.666
GRADE 2, CLASS 1

12:23.749 --> 12:25.376
Hayato's been whining all morning.

12:26.294 --> 12:27.462
Wow.

12:27.545 --> 12:29.881
- Thanks for everything, Hayato.
- You're so heartless!

12:29.964 --> 12:30.965
SCREAM

12:31.048 --> 12:32.049
What's your name?

12:32.133 --> 12:33.134
I'm Tsukiko.

12:33.217 --> 12:34.719
Tsukko then.

12:35.219 --> 12:37.138
I'm Yota. Nice to meet you.

12:37.221 --> 12:38.431
FLOATY

12:38.514 --> 12:39.891
<i>Floating away.</i>

12:44.020 --> 12:45.146
SIGH

12:45.229 --> 12:48.983
<i>It's, like, so lively in there.</i>

12:49.484 --> 12:52.904
<i>It's going to be completely different</i>
<i>from Grade 1, Class 2.</i>

12:53.905 --> 12:56.073
<i>Still, I don't hate it.</i>

12:56.574 --> 12:57.783
Koyun.

12:58.451 --> 13:00.495
Sorry, we didn't mean to push you out.

13:01.120 --> 13:02.872
Were we too loud?

13:03.372 --> 13:05.500
Huh? Not at all.

13:06.250 --> 13:10.046
Just thought there's no point
for me to be in there.

13:10.129 --> 13:12.715
- What?
- Rather, sorry I made you worried.

13:13.216 --> 13:15.426
<i>This is difficult…</i>

13:15.510 --> 13:18.804
HE LOVES CROWDS
SHE LOVES SPACE

13:18.888 --> 13:19.889
GRADE 2, CLASS 3

13:19.972 --> 13:21.682
Is it okay to leave that person alone?

13:21.766 --> 13:23.309
THAT PERSON

13:23.935 --> 13:26.395
He likes to put on his loud comedy act.

13:27.647 --> 13:28.981
A loud comedy act.

13:33.945 --> 13:35.947
Listen…

13:36.030 --> 13:39.909
I'm really glad we're in the same class.

13:43.204 --> 13:44.205
Me too.

13:45.540 --> 13:48.584
You feel more at ease
when there's a familiar face in class.

13:49.544 --> 13:50.711
Right.

13:50.795 --> 13:52.713
A FAMILIAR FACE

13:53.297 --> 13:57.051
- Do you see that guy's hair?
- He's locked in.

13:57.593 --> 14:00.471
Crap, what's my class again?

14:01.097 --> 14:04.892
Second years are in charge
of club introduction skits, right?

14:04.976 --> 14:05.977
Yeah.

14:06.060 --> 14:08.688
I already know it'll be corny
so I don't want to participate.

14:09.188 --> 14:10.231
I want to go watch it.

14:10.314 --> 14:12.567
Seriously, don't come.

14:13.776 --> 14:14.860
Hey!

14:14.944 --> 14:16.195
SQUEEZE

14:19.490 --> 14:20.741
Who is it?

14:21.325 --> 14:22.618
<i>Who is it?</i>

14:24.036 --> 14:25.621
This voice…

14:25.705 --> 14:27.039
Yuki.

14:27.123 --> 14:28.374
Bingo.

14:28.457 --> 14:30.167
That's my Koyun.

14:30.251 --> 14:31.252
<i>Koyun?</i>

14:31.335 --> 14:33.754
You're the only one
who'd pull a prank like this.

14:33.838 --> 14:35.047
<i>They're friends?</i>

14:35.548 --> 14:38.342
<i>That's fine,</i>
<i>but get your hand off her already.</i>

14:40.511 --> 14:43.222
Amamiya, meet Yuki.

14:43.306 --> 14:44.432
He's Miki's younger brother.

14:44.515 --> 14:47.018
What's up? I'm Yuki Azumi.

14:47.101 --> 14:49.687
Huh? Miki's brother?

14:50.313 --> 14:51.564
He's my younger brother.

14:51.647 --> 14:54.942
We grew up together,
and he's her childhood friend.

14:55.026 --> 14:56.777
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

14:56.861 --> 14:59.280
Amamiya?

14:59.363 --> 15:01.282
Could you be Minato?

15:01.365 --> 15:03.659
- What?
- I totally know you.

15:03.743 --> 15:05.620
Miki's mentioned your name before.

15:05.703 --> 15:06.704
It's rude to point.

15:06.787 --> 15:09.540
Thanks for being good to my sister.

15:10.124 --> 15:11.834
Man, you're a solid 10!

15:11.918 --> 15:13.836
- Wait, what?
- Oh, I know.

15:13.920 --> 15:15.796
Are you guys in Miki's class?

15:15.880 --> 15:17.548
GRADE 2, CLASS 2

15:17.632 --> 15:18.633
STILL HANGING AROUND

15:18.716 --> 15:20.176
Midorikawa, you're from Kansai?

15:20.259 --> 15:21.677
I moved out here for high school.

15:21.761 --> 15:23.346
I love Kansai dialect.

15:23.429 --> 15:24.430
Do you actually?

15:24.513 --> 15:27.642
I wanna say,
"What's up with that?" and stuff.

15:27.725 --> 15:29.769
Your Kansai dialect's all messed up.

15:30.311 --> 15:31.520
Miki!

15:32.146 --> 15:33.606
Heya!

15:33.689 --> 15:35.566
- What's up with that?
- You're using it.

15:35.650 --> 15:37.193
Yuki!

15:37.276 --> 15:38.986
I told you to leave me alone at school!

15:39.070 --> 15:40.446
I'm gonna bother you anyway.

15:40.529 --> 15:41.572
Anyway, here.

15:41.656 --> 15:44.408
Your lunch. You forgot it again.

15:45.034 --> 15:46.035
COMPLETE 180

15:46.118 --> 15:47.119
Thanks, Yuki.

15:47.203 --> 15:48.245
Be grateful.

15:48.788 --> 15:51.248
You don't come to school together?

15:51.332 --> 15:54.794
Nope. Yuki takes forever
getting ready, styling his hair and stuff.

15:54.877 --> 15:57.213
Well, you know…

15:57.296 --> 15:58.297
HMPH

15:58.381 --> 15:59.715
Can't have people lookin' down on me.

15:59.799 --> 16:02.218
You sound like a country bumpkin
delinquent. Knock it off!

16:02.885 --> 16:04.679
- Yuki.
- Yeah?

16:04.762 --> 16:06.973
Think you can make friends?

16:07.056 --> 16:09.225
WHAT? EXPRESSION
FOR "YOU'RE ONE TO TALK"

16:09.308 --> 16:12.478
There's someone I went to middle school
with in my class. I'm not worried.

16:13.229 --> 16:14.355
Good for you.

16:14.438 --> 16:17.858
<i>It's like… she's more composed than usual.</i>

16:17.942 --> 16:20.444
RIGHT NOW - TALKING CASUALLY
USUAL - TIMID AND CAREFUL

16:20.528 --> 16:22.738
<i>She can talk to him</i>
<i>without feeling anxious.</i>

16:22.822 --> 16:24.490
Before I forget.

16:24.573 --> 16:25.950
Come with me, Yuki.

16:26.033 --> 16:27.368
Whoa!

16:27.451 --> 16:29.120
What is it?

16:31.664 --> 16:32.873
Yota.

16:33.457 --> 16:36.043
This is Yuki. He's Miki's younger brother.

16:37.211 --> 16:39.213
You're right. I see the resemblance.

16:39.296 --> 16:40.756
You're massive!

16:40.840 --> 16:42.341
I've heard of you, Yota.

16:43.217 --> 16:45.428
Miki told me about you.

16:45.511 --> 16:46.971
About me?

16:47.471 --> 16:49.015
- Seriously, you're huge.
- Sheesh.

16:49.098 --> 16:51.642
- Train rides must be comfortable.
- She doesn't need to introduce him.

16:51.726 --> 16:53.644
Koyun said the same thing.

16:53.728 --> 16:56.105
He can reach higher than the handrails.

16:56.188 --> 16:57.356
Man, I'm jealous.

17:00.026 --> 17:01.277
<i>Those two…</i>

17:02.528 --> 17:04.613
<i>share a special bond.</i>

17:04.697 --> 17:05.906
<i>Meanwhile, I'm…</i>

17:05.990 --> 17:08.993
You feel more at ease
when there's a familiar face in class.

17:09.577 --> 17:12.830
<i>And she dated Igarashi in the past.</i>

17:15.207 --> 17:16.709
<i>What am I going to do?</i>

17:17.460 --> 17:20.212
<i>I wanted to be genuine friends,</i>
<i>I wanted her to smile…</i>

17:20.713 --> 17:24.008
<i>But there's more to it than</i>
<i>these pure motivations now.</i>

17:27.011 --> 17:31.766
<i>I wish she would only like me.</i>

17:34.685 --> 17:37.188
Hey, guys! Let's all sign up
for the sports festival's cheer squad.

17:37.271 --> 17:38.272
CHEER SQUAD
RECRUITING MEMBERS

17:38.355 --> 17:39.607
Why?

17:39.690 --> 17:42.318
Last year, I passed on it,

17:42.401 --> 17:45.237
then ended up regretting it on the day of.

17:45.321 --> 17:47.990
I told myself I'd do it next time.

17:48.074 --> 17:50.159
So what do you say, guys?

17:50.242 --> 17:51.452
Okay, sure.

17:51.952 --> 17:54.121
- Why not?
- Yes!

17:54.205 --> 17:56.123
You'll join too, right, Minato?

17:56.749 --> 17:58.042
Yeah.

17:59.293 --> 18:00.628
I can't wait!

18:00.711 --> 18:02.713
- A cheer squad full of friends!
- Amazing.

18:02.797 --> 18:05.633
- This is the best!
- They agreed to that easily.

18:05.716 --> 18:07.343
- Now, only one left is…
- That's Miki for you.

18:07.426 --> 18:11.305
Koyun! We're gonna join
the cheer squad! Yeah!

18:11.388 --> 18:13.390
I heard you.

18:13.474 --> 18:15.559
It might be a lot of work, but good luck.

18:16.310 --> 18:17.645
What?

18:22.942 --> 18:23.943
LOOKY

18:24.777 --> 18:26.278
BAM

18:26.779 --> 18:27.780
Why me?

18:28.280 --> 18:29.281
Sorry.

18:29.365 --> 18:32.159
All right, first and second years.

18:32.243 --> 18:35.454
If you haven't memorized
the first part, come over here.

18:35.538 --> 18:37.123
SELF-PRACTICE TIME

18:37.206 --> 18:38.207
Why's Hayato here?

18:38.290 --> 18:40.209
Class 1 and 2 are in the same squad.
Act happy!

18:40.292 --> 18:41.460
HERE
BLUE SQUAD - CLASS 1 AND 2

18:41.544 --> 18:42.545
WINGING IT

18:42.628 --> 18:44.839
Go swoosh, swoosh, then boom.

18:45.422 --> 18:46.423
Koyun.

18:47.049 --> 18:48.968
Want me to teach you
the parts you don't know?

18:49.051 --> 18:50.052
GASP

18:50.136 --> 18:51.220
A scary guy came over!

18:51.303 --> 18:53.722
- Don't be afraid.
- What?

18:53.806 --> 18:55.558
Meet Yuki, Miki's younger brother.

18:55.641 --> 18:56.684
Good to meet ya!

18:56.767 --> 18:57.768
PHEW

18:57.852 --> 18:59.478
- Oh, I see.
- Don't introduce him.

18:59.562 --> 19:01.355
Shoo! Off you go.

19:01.438 --> 19:02.648
Why?

19:02.731 --> 19:04.650
- Just go!
- She's scaring me.

19:04.733 --> 19:06.360
Help me, Koyun.

19:06.443 --> 19:07.987
Don't fight, you two.

19:08.070 --> 19:09.989
Guess I've gotta leave now.

19:10.072 --> 19:11.407
Now start walking!

19:11.490 --> 19:12.658
Bye!

19:12.741 --> 19:13.993
See you, Yuki.

19:16.996 --> 19:17.997
POKE

19:18.622 --> 19:21.041
Practice ended earlier than we thought.

19:21.125 --> 19:22.543
Your finger…

19:22.626 --> 19:23.627
GEEZ

19:23.711 --> 19:25.838
I just exercised, so my face is sweaty.

19:25.921 --> 19:27.506
That's what makes you upset?

19:27.590 --> 19:28.591
STARE

19:28.674 --> 19:30.759
- Do you have club activities after this?
- Yeah.

19:31.260 --> 19:33.262
You've got cheer squad
and your club? That's tough.

19:33.345 --> 19:34.680
Not really.

19:34.763 --> 19:35.764
<i>What's this?</i>

19:36.724 --> 19:38.017
<i>Is this what I think it is?</i>

19:39.310 --> 19:40.519
<i>Could this be…</i>

19:40.603 --> 19:43.355
<i>Am I third-wheeling?</i>

19:43.856 --> 19:45.774
SWISH

19:45.858 --> 19:46.942
Are you in a club, Shimojima?

19:47.026 --> 19:48.027
JOLT!

19:48.110 --> 19:49.695
<i>He's talking to me now!</i>

19:49.778 --> 19:51.697
I-I'm in art club.

19:51.780 --> 19:53.782
Were you in the cheer squad last year?

19:53.866 --> 19:57.286
<i>It's fine, Amamiya.</i>
<i>You don't have to include me.</i>

19:57.369 --> 19:59.288
I talked her into it.

19:59.371 --> 20:01.248
- <i>What should I do?</i>
- How do you two know each other?

20:01.332 --> 20:03.876
- <i>I'd hate to be a third wheel…</i>
- Last year, in March…

20:03.959 --> 20:05.544
<i>…but I do want to keep watching.</i>

20:05.628 --> 20:07.796
CURIOSITY - BEING CONSIDERATE
HEE, HEE

20:08.881 --> 20:13.052
Goodness. I'm so done with practice!

20:13.135 --> 20:14.511
I'm wiped.

20:14.595 --> 20:16.222
It's only the first day.

20:16.305 --> 20:18.641
Try to be more like
the energetic kids chatting over there.

20:18.724 --> 20:19.725
CHATTER, CHATTER

20:19.808 --> 20:22.061
You mean the first years?

20:22.561 --> 20:25.814
Yeah, lots of flashy kids this year.

20:25.898 --> 20:26.899
NEAR-SIGHTED

20:26.982 --> 20:30.069
What's goin' on with Meiten?
This isn't our usual cohort.

20:30.152 --> 20:34.281
That reminds me.
Earlier, I spotted two flashy students

20:34.365 --> 20:36.325
who looked like celebrities.

20:36.408 --> 20:38.244
- Seriously? Where?
- Right there.

20:38.327 --> 20:39.328
NEAR-SIGHTED

20:39.411 --> 20:40.955
See them?

20:41.038 --> 20:44.375
The tall one with the bun
and the one with long hair.

20:45.000 --> 20:46.460
Practice is done.

20:46.543 --> 20:49.463
What're you gonna do, Akine?
Are you going home?

20:50.381 --> 20:51.423
Not quite.

20:51.507 --> 20:53.217
Momoka, you go home without me.

20:54.385 --> 20:56.971
There's someone I want to meet.

20:58.222 --> 20:59.223
See you.

21:06.188 --> 21:08.190
Does the library ever get busy?

21:08.274 --> 21:10.192
Not really.

21:10.276 --> 21:13.570
<i>That girl… she's staring right at us.</i>

21:18.200 --> 21:19.368
Heya.

21:20.327 --> 21:23.122
- You stopped by about the manager role.
- Yes.

21:23.205 --> 21:25.624
<i>I guess she's</i>
<i>an acquaintance of Amamiya's.</i>

21:26.208 --> 21:27.710
Will you be coming after this today?

21:27.793 --> 21:30.004
Yes. I look forward to seeing you there.

21:48.105 --> 21:50.649
Koyuki Yuishiro.

21:51.734 --> 21:52.985
<i>Yuishiro?</i>

21:53.485 --> 21:57.406
Huh? Atagawa, do you know Hikawa?

21:58.324 --> 21:59.658
Atagawa…

22:00.242 --> 22:01.243
Yes.

22:01.327 --> 22:02.911
I'm Akine Atagawa.

22:03.829 --> 22:06.206
I'm from the same middle school as Azumi.

22:06.290 --> 22:09.001
I heard all about you, Koyuki.

22:09.543 --> 22:11.920
<i>Akine Atagawa…</i>

22:12.546 --> 22:13.630
<i>She can't be…</i>

22:15.215 --> 22:18.677
I look forward to getting to know you.

22:19.511 --> 22:20.929
<i>She's Manatsu Atagawa's…</i>

22:22.139 --> 22:23.182
<i>younger sister…</i>

23:50.269 --> 23:55.274
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
